  "content": "Minister Ghising inspects flood and landslide affected zone\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 12, 2025\n0\nComments\nFikkal (Ilam), October 12\nMinister for Urban Development, Energy, Water Resources and Irrigation, as well as Physical Infrastructure and Transport, Kulman Ghising, has reaffirmed the government’s commitment to prioritize rehabilitation efforts in regions impacted by floods and landslides.\nDuring a meeting with stakeholders organized by the District Disaster Management Committee at the District Administration Office in Ilam on October 11, Minister Ghising emphasized that since Ilam has been designated a ‘disaster-emergency area,’ rehabilitation initiatives will be given utmost priority.\nAfter the inspection in the affected areas, he also declared that the reconstruction of damaged motorable bridges, Bailey bridges, and suspension bridges would be expedited.\nIn Ilam, the recent floods and landslides have caused damages to 19 motorable bridges, two Bailey bridges, and three suspension bridges. Chief District Officer Sunita Nepal reported that the floods and landslides in Ilam resulted in 39 fatalities, 26 injuries, and one person missing.\nConsequently, 276 families were displaced, 151 houses were completely destroyed, and 327 houses sustained partial damage.\n—RSS\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\ngold\nnepali cricket\nflood\nSushila Karki\ninsurance\nICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\nKapan\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nFloods and landslides disrupt roads and power supply in Kavrepalanchok\n5 days ago\nFloods block Maidhar–Dudhe section of Asian Highway in Jhapa\n1 week ago\nIPPAN calls for high alert over flood threat\n3 months ago\n55 rescued, 18 missing after flood hits Rasuwagadhi\n3 months ago\nFlood alert issued as water 